      "message": "List who never came, and let them go\n\nAn invited person was a full principal at once and held the name for\ngood; the ones who never followed their link showed as \"no password\nyet\" on the People page and nowhere else, and nothing ever cleared\nthem. The door now lists them — GET /api/invitations/unclaimed: the\nactive people nobody has ever been, each with when their newest\ninvitation lapses — and POST /api/invitations/purge lets go those\nwhose invitation has lapsed: deactivated and their invitations\nrevoked, each on the record, as whoever asked. `cairn admin\nunclaimed --purge` does the same offline. A name stays on the log;\nwhoever runs the forge can reactivate an account that turns up after\nall.\n\nChange-Id: Iunclaimed0118\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
